WEBVTT - AeroSense AI Product Demonstration Subtitles

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.799
Air pollution is one of the most critical public health emergencies of our time.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:13.800
Across South Asia and the Indo-Gangetic Plain, hundreds of millions wake up under thick winter smog.

3
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:25.800
Knowing the air is 'Unhealthy' doesn't tell a mother when to open windows, or an asthmatic grandfather his inhaled particulate mass.

4
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:37.799
Welcome to AeroSense AI — the Clean-Air Decision Engine, built for PromptWars Challenge 6.

5
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:50.129
Our mission: Know the air. Predict the risk. Protect your family. Prove the impact.

6
00:00:50.329 --> 00:00:59.129
To see how AeroSense AI works in the real world, let's follow the Sharma family in Bengaluru.

7
00:00:59.329 --> 00:01:11.129
The parents commute on Outer Ring Road, 8-year-old Aarav has soccer practice, and Grandfather plans his daily walk.

8
00:01:11.329 --> 00:01:21.129
Is outdoor air safe for soccer? Is pollution trapping closer to the ground? Should they ventilate or seal?

9
00:01:21.329 --> 00:01:30.519
Traditional apps just give a number. AeroSense AI guides their decisions from sunrise to bedtime.

10
00:01:30.719 --> 00:01:38.519
Here is the AeroSense AI platform, live on the web at aero-sense-ai-psi.vercel.app.

11
00:01:38.719 --> 00:01:47.519
Deep ink slate accented by emerald and cyan, designed for high contrast and accessibility.

12
00:01:47.719 --> 00:01:57.519
Our deterministic engines do all the science. Generative AI only plans and explains.

13
00:01:57.719 --> 00:02:08.520
Every metric is grounded in verified physics with zero hallucinated numbers. Let's launch the dashboard.

14
00:02:08.719 --> 00:02:13.520
We are now inside the Overview Dashboard.

15
00:02:13.719 --> 00:02:24.520
Right now in Bengaluru, our deterministic engine calculates an Indian National AQI of 139 (Moderate).

16
00:02:24.719 --> 00:02:36.520
The dominant pollutant is Ozone (O3) at 127 µg/m³, while PM2.5 is clean at 24.2 µg/m³.

17
00:02:36.719 --> 00:02:48.520
Our 3D atmospheric scene shows a convective boundary-layer height of 1,045 meters.

18
00:02:48.719 --> 00:03:00.520
With winds at 11.8 km/h, the Inversion Risk Score is low — just 24 out of 100.

19
00:03:00.719 --> 00:03:13.259
The Telemetry strip displays live Open-Meteo reanalysis, CPCB engines, and station status.

20
00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:24.259
Pillar 1: Live Air Intelligence. Inspect PM2.5, PM10, NO2, SO2, CO, and Ozone.

21
00:03:24.459 --> 00:03:35.259
Every sub-index is computed strictly according to CPCB October 2014 guidelines.

22
00:03:35.459 --> 00:03:46.259
Switching from Bengaluru to Delhi-NCR in the selector updates the entire dashboard.

23
00:03:46.459 --> 00:04:04.769
Delhi surges to AQI 255 (Poor) dominated by PM2.5 at 106.9 µg/m³ — over 4x higher than Bengaluru.

24
00:04:04.969 --> 00:04:10.769
Pillar 2: Pollution Forecast and Atmospheric Risk.

25
00:04:10.969 --> 00:04:21.769
During cold winter evenings, thermal inversions trap pollution near ground level.

26
00:04:21.969 --> 00:04:35.769
Our lapse rate engine analyzes surface, 925 hPa, and 850 hPa temperatures to detect traps hours ahead.

27
00:04:35.969 --> 00:04:48.769
Our Backtest Calibration Panel transparently reports MAE, RMSE, and bias against historical readings.

28
00:04:48.969 --> 00:04:59.879
We never claim a model is 100% accurate; we show its actual physical uncertainty.

29
00:05:00.079 --> 00:05:13.879
Pillar 3: Family Protection. All profiles, ages, and medical sensitivities are stored strictly on-device in IndexedDB.

30
00:05:14.079 --> 00:05:24.879
Personal identifiers are stripped before any LLM call, passing only anonymized age groups.

31
00:05:25.079 --> 00:05:36.879
AeroSense AI calculates inhaled dose: Concentration times minute ventilation rate times duration.

32
00:05:37.079 --> 00:05:48.879
Aarav's soccer dose is 13.3 micrograms — only 6% of his WHO daily recommended limit of 225 micrograms.

33
00:05:49.079 --> 00:06:02.209
Grandfather's respiratory risk in Bengaluru equals less than 0.1 cigarettes equivalent today.

34
00:06:02.409 --> 00:06:13.209
Pillar 4: Indoor Air Advisor. Most people spend 90% of their lives indoors.

35
00:06:13.409 --> 00:06:25.209
Our first-principles PM2.5 Mass-Balance model evaluates infiltration, settling, and filtration.

36
00:06:25.409 --> 00:06:37.209
In Bengaluru (PM2.5 24.2 µg/m³), the engine recommends 'Open Windows for Natural Ventilation'.

37
00:06:37.409 --> 00:06:49.209
In Delhi (PM2.5 106.9 µg/m³), the equation reverses: 'Seal Windows and Run Purifier'.

38
00:06:49.409 --> 00:07:02.289
Includes CADR purifier sizing and DIY open-source Corsi-Rosenthal Box blueprints.

39
00:07:02.489 --> 00:07:12.289
Pillar 5: Act — The What-If Simulator. Proving the measurable impact of sustainable choices.

40
00:07:12.489 --> 00:07:25.289
Shifting Priya's 15 km commute from a petrol scooter to Namma Metro drops emissions by 97.5%.

41
00:07:25.489 --> 00:07:34.289
Clicking View Impact Receipt generates an auditable scientific receipt.

42
00:07:34.489 --> 00:07:48.309
Shows baseline, delta with units, emission factors, confidence, and engine version impact@1.0.0.

43
00:07:48.509 --> 00:07:58.309
AeroSense Drone Lab — Custom hardware for vertical atmospheric profiling.

44
00:07:58.509 --> 00:08:10.309
Radical honesty: connection status shows 'Not Connected' while the prototype is in the workshop.

45
00:08:10.509 --> 00:08:21.309
Clicking Launch Flight Demonstration illuminates an explicit 'SIMULATED' badge.

46
00:08:21.509 --> 00:08:36.159
The telemetry HUD animates quadcopter ascent up to 120m, mapping vertical boundary layer traps.

47
00:08:36.359 --> 00:08:44.159
Community Hub: Individual actions scale to neighborhood impact.

48
00:08:44.359 --> 00:08:56.159
Clean-Air Decision Score (0-100) measures verified household mitigation actions, never biological health.

49
00:08:56.359 --> 00:09:07.769
Provides Sectoral Action Plans for schools, eldercare homes, and construction sites.

50
00:09:07.969 --> 00:09:16.769
AeroSense AI Copilot powered by Google Gemini 2.5 Flash.

51
00:09:16.969 --> 00:09:28.769
Prompts are sanitized, PII is stripped, and Gemini receives verified deterministic facts.

52
00:09:28.969 --> 00:09:42.769
When asked about outdoor soccer, Gemini cites Fact #1: AQI 139 and Fact #3: PM2.5 24.2 µg/m³.

53
00:09:42.969 --> 00:10:02.949
Server-side validation audits all numbers in the LLM response, rejecting unsupported claims.

54
00:10:03.149 --> 00:10:13.949
Clean-Air Daily Planner synthesizes all intelligence into a personalized 24-hour routine.

55
00:10:14.149 --> 00:10:30.659
Schedules 7 AM ventilation, 8:30 AM metro commute, 1-4 PM outdoor window, and 7 PM evening seal.

56
00:10:30.859 --> 00:10:42.659
Spatial Air and Incident Map at /map. Concentric radar rings at 10, 25, and 50 kilometers.

57
00:10:42.859 --> 00:10:54.659
Wind indicator shows 11.8 km/h from Northeast towards 226° Southwest with 35° downwind plume sector.

58
00:10:54.859 --> 00:11:10.109
Satellite fire points are labeled thermal indicators; downwind zones are explicitly mathematical estimates.

59
00:11:10.309 --> 00:11:20.109
Under the hood: 5-layer decoupled architecture powering AeroSense AI.

60
00:11:20.309 --> 00:11:32.109
Layer 1: Multi-source ingestion. Layer 2: Fusion, privacy, and safety gateway.

61
00:11:32.309 --> 00:11:45.109
Layer 3: Eight deterministic engines running 100% offline with zero LLM dependencies.

62
00:11:45.309 --> 00:12:00.109
Layer 4: Fact Registry and Impact Receipts. Layer 5: Next.js 15, Three.js 3D, and 11 Indian languages.

63
00:12:00.309 --> 00:12:13.109
120 passing Vitest tests. Developed by Somashekhar Vani for PromptWars Challenge 6.

64
00:12:13.309 --> 00:12:27.449
AeroSense AI: Know the air. Predict the risk. Protect your family. Prove the impact.

